p_begin_timing_events_cache\", None)\n        if cache is None:\n            cache = {}\n            self._frozen_split_decomp_begin_timing_events_cache = cache\n        key = (layer_id, name) if group is None else (layer_id, name, group)\n        ev = cache.get(key)\n        if ev is None:\n            ev = torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True, external=True)\n            ev.record()\n            cache[key] = ev\n        return ev\n\n    def _frozen_split_decomp_end_timing_event(self, layer_id: int,\n                                                name: str,\n                                                group=None\n                                                ) -> torch.cuda.Event:\n        \"\"\"END timing marker paired with the BEGIN above.\"\"\"\n        cache = getattr(\n            self, \"_frozen_split_decomp_end_timing_events_cache\", None)\n        if cache is None:\n            cache = {}\n            self._frozen_split_decomp_end_timing_events_cache = cache\n        key = (layer_id, name) if group is None else (layer_id, name, group)\n        ev = cache.get(key)\n        if ev is None:\n            ev = torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True, external=True)\n            ev.record()\n            cache[key] = ev\n        return ev\n\n    def _ensure_graph_replay_end_events(self, n_graphs: int\n                                        ) -> List[torch.cuda.Event]:\n        \"\"\"Lazy per-graph_idx event recorded on cur_stream at the end of\n        ``_after_replay(K)`` to mark graph K's GPU-side completion.\n        decomp_weight_stream waits on event[K-1] before launching graph\n        K+1's decomp in ``_before_replay(K)`` so it doesn't write to a\n        parity-K%3 buffer that an older in-flight graph (e.g. graph\n        K-3, parity (K-3)%3 = K%3) is still reading.\"\"\"\n        cache = getattr(self, \"_graph_replay_end_events\", None)\n        if cache is None or len(cache) < n_graphs:\n            cache = []\n            for _ in range(n_graphs):\n                ev = torch.cuda.Event(external=True)\n                ev.record()  # initial value satisfied\n                cache.append(ev)\n            self._graph_replay_end_events = cache\n        return cache\n\n    def _ensure_graph_decomp_done_events(self, n_graphs: int\n                                         ) -> List[torch.cuda.Event]:\n        \"\"\"Lazy per-graph_idx event used to gate cur_stream's graph K\n        replay on completion of graph K's frozen weight decompress.\n        Decomp for graph K is pre-launched in ``_before_replay(K-1)``\n        so it overlaps with graph K-1 replay + attention K-1.  This\n        event is recorded right after that launch on decomp_weight_stream\n        and waited on cur_stream at the start of graph K's _before_replay.\n        Allocated once on first use, sized to n_graphs.\"\"\"\n        cache = getattr(self, \"_graph_decomp_done_events\", None)\n        if cache is None or len(cache) < n_graphs:\n            cache = []\n            for _ in range(n_graphs):\n                ev = torch.cuda.Event(external=True)\n                ev.record()  # initial value satisfied\n                cache.append(ev)\n            self._graph_decomp_done_events = cache\n        return cache\n\n    def _frozen_split_kernel_done_event(self, layer_id: int, name: str\n                                        ) -> torch.cuda.Event:\n        \"\"\"Lazy event recorded after each frozen-split decompress kernel.\n\n        The staging buffers are keyed by ``(name, layer_id % parity)``, not by\n        absolute layer id.  Lookahead can therefore schedule layer K+2 while\n        layer K's kernel is still reading the same staging slot.  Gate H2D on\n        the previous kernel for the same physical staging slot.\n        \"\"\"\n        cache = getattr(self, \"_frozen_split_kernel_done_events\", None)\n        if cache is None:\n            cache = {}\n            free_by_name = self._frozen_split_alt_staging_free_events = {}\n        h2d_by_name = getattr(\n            self, \"_frozen_split_alt_h2d_done_events\", None)\n        if h2d_by_name is None:\n            h2d_by_name = self._frozen_split_alt_h2d_done_events = {}\n\n        free_events = free_by_name.setdefault(name, [])\n        h2d_events = h2d_by_name.setdefault(name, [])\n        while len(free_events) < self.FROZEN_STAGING_PARITY:\n            free = torch.cuda.Event(external=True)\n            free.record()  # first occupant has no prior decoder to wait for\n            free_events.append(free)\n            h2d_events.append(torch.cuda.Event(external=True))\n\n    def _materialize_frozen_split_prefill_alt(\n            self, layer_id, name, alt, output, alt_comp):\n        \"\"\"Stage one eager-prefill alt weight without blocking compute H2D.\n\n        The wrapper schedules a future NONE-path piece after the current piece\n        has been submitted. Putting only these copies on load_weight_stream lets\n        them overlap that current compute. The H2D-done wait and decoder remain\n        on exec afterwards, ordered before the future component-ready event and\n        consuming GEMM.\n        \"\"\"\n        parity = layer_id % self.FROZEN_STAGING_PARITY\n        alt_staging = self.frozen_split_alt_staging[name][parity]\n        staging_free = self._frozen_split_alt_staging_free_events[name][parity]\n        h2d_done = self._frozen_split_alt_h2d_done_events[name][parity]\n\n        # Do not overwrite this parity slot while its previous P4 decoder is\n        # still reading it.\n        self.load_weight_stream.wait_event(staging_free)\n        tb = self.time_breakdown\n        with torch.cuda.stream(self.load_weight_stream):\n            if tb:\n                self._frozen_split_h2d_begin_event(\n                    layer_id, name).record(self.load_weight_stream)\n            for attr in alt.lpddr_attrs:\n                ne = alt.lpddr_numels[attr]\n                alt_staging[attr][:ne].copy_(\n                    alt.lpddr_buffers[attr], non_blocking=True)\n            if tb:\n                self._frozen_split_h2d_end_timing_event(\n                    layer_id, name).record(self.load_weight_stream)\n            h2d_done.record(self.load_weight_stream)\n\n        # Keep P4 decode and its dense output on exec/current. Moving the decoder\n        # itself would add SM contention and a second cross-stream WAR on the\n        # parity-shared dense primary buffer.\n        self.decomp_weight_stream.wait_event(h2d_done)\n        if tb:\n            self._frozen_split_decomp_begin_timing_event(\n                layer_id, name).record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n        self._frozen_split_run_decompress(\n            alt, alt_staging, alt.lpddr_numels, output, alt_comp)\n        if tb:\n            self._frozen_split_decomp_end_timing_event(\n                layer_id, name).record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n        staging_free.record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _parse_prefill_alt_max_chunk(raw, default=None):\n        \"\"\"Parse TIERED_SERVE_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK into (per_backend, fallback).\n\n        Accepts a single int (one global override for every codec) or a comma\n        list of \"<codec>=<n>\" entries plus an optional bare int that overrides\n        the default for codecs not explicitly named. Codec keys are lower-cased\n        to match SplitStorageInfo.backend. Whitespace around tokens is ignored.\n\n        ``fallback`` stays ``None`` unless the env contained a bare int. None\n        signals \"unset\", so ``_alt_max_chunk_for`` then consults the built-in\n            # Move the (large, 2*M*K) raw H2D OFF exec onto load_weight_stream so\n            # the slow C2C copy overlaps the prefill GEMMs instead of serialising\n            # on exec (decomp_weight_stream == exec_stream).  This is only\n            # correct when the consuming graph has a per-component readiness\n            # wait, either from the FX pass or directly in the fused custom op.\n            _component_waits = (\n                (getattr(type(self), \"_v1_weight_waits_active\", False)\n                 or getattr(self, \"_v1_fused_weight_waits_complete\", False))\n                and comp_key is not None\n                and hasattr(self, \"frozen_decomp_events\")\n            )\n            if _component_waits:\n                # The primary buffer `output` is now written cross-stream, so\n                # guard it with the WAR events.\n                self._ensure_prefill_war_events()\n                war = self._prefill_war_events.get(comp_key)\n                P = self.FROZEN_DECOMP_PARITY\n                if war is not None:\n                    # Default path: free the prior layer's slot for this comp\n                    # inline.  V1 prefill eager lookahead disables this record\n                    # and lets the wrapper mark slots free after the eager piece\n                    # actually consumes them; otherwise scheduling graph K+1\n                    # before graph K would falsely free graph K's qkv slot.\n                    if not getattr(self, \"_v1_prefill_raw_external_war\",\n                                   False):\n                        war[(layer_id - 1) % P].record(self.exec_stream)\n                    # WAR: this H2D overwrites slot L%P, last read by layer\n                    # (L-PARITY)'s GEMM.  Layers < PARITY are first occupants\n                    # (fresh buffer) → no prior reader → skip.\n                    if layer_id >= P:\n                        self.load_weight_stream.wait_event(war[layer_id % P])\n                with torch.cuda.stream(self.load_weight_stream):\n                    output.view(src.shape).copy_(src, non_blocking=True)\n                # RAW: record weight-ready on load_weight_stream so the FX\n                # wait_frozen_weight makes the GEMM wait for THIS H2D.  Suppress\n                # the caller's default exec-stream record (it would shadow this\n                # with an already-complete event → torn weight read).\n                self.frozen_decomp_events[comp_key][layer_id].record(\n                    self.load_weight_stream)\n                self._last_prefill_raw_recorded = True\n            else:\n                # Fallback: move H2D off exec_stream onto load_weight_stream\n                # so the copy overlaps compute instead of blocking the GEMM\n                # stream.  The caller records frozen_decomp_events on\n                # decomp_weight_stream after this returns; the wait_stream\n                # below ensures that event fires only after the H2D completes.\n                with torch.cuda.stream(self.load_weight_stream):\n                    output.view(src.shape).copy_(src, non_blocking=True)\n                self.decomp_weight_stream.wait_stream(\n                    self.load_weight_stream)\n            if detailed_nvtx:\n                torch.cuda.nvtx.range_pop()\n            return\n\n        # Decode path: H2D on load_weight_stream, decompress kernel on\n        # decomp_weight_stream, fused via per-(layer,name) events.\n        #\n        # Sync model:\n        #   * H2D waits on kernel_done[name, parity] from the previous\n        #     use of the same physical staging slot so it doesn't overwrite\n        #     `staging` while the prior kernel is still reading it.\n        #   * Kernel waits on h2d_event[layer,name] for *this* H2D only,\n        #     so the next tensor's H2D can run concurrently with this\n        #     kernel on the decompress stream.\n        kernel_done_event = self._frozen_split_kernel_done_event(\n            layer_id, name)\n        # Timing events (h2d_begin/end, split_decomp begin/end) are consumed\n        # only by the --time-breakdown diagnostic.  Fetch + record them only\n        # when it's enabled so the decode hot path stays event-light.\n        tb = self.time_breakdown\n\n        if self._ats_decomp_frozen:\n            # ATS path: the LPDDR hugepage is already cudaHostRegister-\n            # mapped, so the GPU kernel dereferences the host pointer\n            # directly via ATS / NVLink-C2C UVA. No H2D, no staging.\n            if not getattr(self, \"_ats_decomp_logged\", False):\n                sample = info.lpddr_buffers[info.lpddr_attrs[0]]\n                logger.info(\n                    \"[ATS-decomp] first decompress L%d.%s src device=%s \"\n                    \"ptr=0x%x\",\n                    layer_id, name, sample.device, sample.data_ptr())\n                self._ats_decomp_logged = True\n\n            if skip_kernel:\n                # ATS + fused_mm: there is no GPU staging slot to populate\n                # (the kernel was going to read straight from LPDDR via\n                # ATS).  fused_mm reads the same LPDDR buffers via the\n                # shell built at install time, so nothing happens here.\n                # ``kernel_done_event`` is recorded by the custom op\n                # after fused_mm completes.\n                return\n\n            if detailed_nvtx:\n                torch.cuda.nvtx.range_push(\n                    f\"frozen_split_{info.backend}_decomp_ats \"\n                    f\"L{layer_id}.{name}\")\n            # Timing BEGIN/END around the decompress kernel for the\n            # time-breakdown only.  Caller already set decomp_weight_stream\n            # as current; record on that stream explicitly to match\n            # H2D-side instrumentation semantics.\n            if tb:\n                self._frozen_split_decomp_begin_timing_event(\n                    layer_id, name).record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n            self._frozen_split_run_decompress(\n                info, info.lpddr_buffers, info.lpddr_numels,\n                output, backend_compressor)\n            if tb:\n                self._frozen_split_decomp_end_timing_event(\n                    layer_id, name).record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n            if detailed_nvtx:\n                torch.cuda.nvtx.range_pop()\n            kernel_done_event.record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n            return\n\n        h2d_event = self._frozen_split_h2d_event(layer_id, name)\n        # Block this H2D against the previous use of the same physical\n        # staging slot.  DIAGNOSTIC (WLOAD_GRAPH): skip during cudagraph capture\n        # — waiting on an external event (kernel_done, recorded outside this\n        # capture) can detach load_weight from the capture so the H2D below is\n        # not recorded into the graph (replay then never loads -> stale weights).\n        if (not _ENV_ANY_WLOAD_GRAPH\n                or not torch.cuda.is_current_stream_capturing()):\n            self.load_weight_stream.wait_event(kernel_done_event)\n        if tb:\n            h2d_begin = self._frozen_split_h2d_begin_event(layer_id, name)\n            h2d_end_timing = self._frozen_split_h2d_end_timing_event(\n                layer_id, name)\n        # Pipeline the (zipserv BF16) H2D + decode in row-tile groups so\n        # group g+1's H2D overlaps group g's decode.  Disabled for the\n        # fused_mm (skip_kernel) path, which needs the whole staging slot\n        # populated for the matmul to read; QKV/O are left whole.\n        plan = None if skip_kernel else self._zipserv_pipeline_plan(\n            info, self.tensor_to_component.get(name))\n\n        if plan is None and collect_into is not None:\n            # #8 batched H2D: defer the copy + h2d_event.record + decomp\n            # wait_event to the caller, which issues ONE batch_memcpy for ALL\n            # projections then records each event.  The WAR guard\n            # (load_weight_stream.wait_event(kernel_done_event)) already ran\n            # above, so the staging slot is safe to overwrite.\n            single = getattr(info, \"_zs_single_slices\", None)\n            if single is None:\n                single = (\n                    [staging[attr].narrow(0, 0, info.lpddr_numels[attr])\n                     for attr in info.lpddr_attrs],\n                    [info.lpddr_buffers[attr]\n                     for attr in info.lpddr_attrs])\n                info._zs_single_slices = single\n            collect_into.append((single[0], single[1], h2d_event))\n            return\n\n        if plan is None:\n            if detailed_nvtx:\n                torch.cuda.nvtx.range_push(\n                    f\"frozen_split_h2d L{layer_id}.{name}\")\n            # When the caller (decompress_frozen_tensors, all-fused decode path)\n            # already holds the load_weight_stream context for the whole\n            # projection loop, stream(None) is a no-op — the copy below\n            # reads current_stream() = load_weight_stream and the records are\n            # explicit, so we skip the per-projection stream-context churn.\n            with torch.cuda.stream(None if h2d_ctx_held else self.load_weight_stream):\n                # BEGIN/END timing markers for the time-breakdown\n                # diagnostic, paired with the sync h2d_event below.\n                # frozen_split keeps sign_mantissa on HBM but H2D's the\n                # compressed-exp/aux buffers every decode step, so this is\n                # the dominant Weight Load source in frozen_split configs\n                # and was being missed by the per-layer\n                # begin_memcpy_weight_events filter.  Two separate END\n                # events because the sync one (h2d_event) must have\n                # enable_timing=False for cross-stream wait semantics.\n                if tb:\n                    h2d_begin.record(self.load_weight_stream)\n                # Single coalesced H2D for all codec buffers (QKV/O and any\n                # non-pipelined tensor load in one dispatch, not one-per-attr).\n                # dst/src views are fixed across decode steps (parity-stable\n                # staging, fixed lpddr_buffers, fixed numels), so build them\n                # once and cache on info instead of re-slicing every step.\n                single = getattr(info, \"_zs_single_slices\", None)\n                if single is None:\n                    single = (\n                        [staging[attr].narrow(0, 0, info.lpddr_numels[attr])\n                         for attr in info.lpddr_attrs],\n                        [info.lpddr_buffers[attr]\n                         for attr in info.lpddr_attrs])\n                    info._zs_single_slices = single\n                    # Cache the raw dst/src/size arrays alongside the views so\n                    # the batched H2D goes through batch_memcpy_ptrs (no per-call\n                    # tensor->ptr rebuild).  Stable for the same reason the views\n                    # are (parity-fixed staging, immutable LPDDR buffers/numels).\n                    info._zs_ptr_arrays = (\n                        [d.data_ptr() for d in single[0]],\n                        [s.data_ptr() for s in single[1]],\n                        [s.numel() * s.element_size() for s in single[1]])\n                # h2d_ctx_held => caller holds torch.cuda.stream(load_weight_stream),\n                # so current_stream() == load_weight_stream: pass its cached raw\n                # handle and skip the per-call current_stream() driver lookup.\n                _sh = self._lw_stream_handle() if h2d_ctx_held else None\n                self._coalesced_h2d(single[0], single[1],\n                                    info._zs_ptr_arrays, _sh)\n                h2d_event.record(self.load_weight_stream)\n                if tb:\n                    h2d_end_timing.record(self.load_weight_stream)\n            if detailed_nvtx:\n                torch.cuda.nvtx.range_pop()  # frozen_split_h2d\n            if skip_kernel:\n                # fused_mm path: H2D is enough — the kernel that consumes\n                # the staging slot is the fused matmul, fired by the\n                # rewritten Linear forward on exec_stream.  The\n                # ``frozen_decomp_events`` recorded by the caller after we\n                # return is therefore recorded directly on load_weight_stream.\n                # No wait is inserted on exec_stream here; the custom op waits\n                # that component event at the actual point of use.  The reciprocal\n                # ``kernel_done_event`` that gates the *next* H2D writing\n                # this staging slot is recorded by the custom op after\n                # fused_mm completes, not here.\n                return\n\n            # Dense reconstruct runs outside the custom op and therefore needs\n            # the H2D dependency on its execution stream.\n            self.decomp_weight_stream.wait_event(h2d_event)\n\n            if detailed_nvtx:\n                torch.cuda.nvtx.range_push(\n                    f\"frozen_split_{info.backend}_decomp L{layer_id}.{name}\")\n            # Timing BEGIN/END around the decompress kernel for the\n            # time-breakdown only (see ATS path above for rationale).\n            if tb:\n                self._frozen_split_decomp_begin_timing_event(\n                    layer_id, name).record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n            self._frozen_split_run_decompress(\n                info, staging, info.lpddr_numels,\n                output, backend_compressor)\n            if tb:\n                self._frozen_split_decomp_end_timing_event(\n                    layer_id, name).record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n            if detailed_nvtx:\n                torch.cuda.nvtx.range_pop()\n            # Record kernel completion on decomp_weight_stream so the *next*\n            # decode step's H2D for this same (layer,name) can wait on it\n            # before overwriting `staging`.\n            kernel_done_event.record(self.decomp_weight_stream)\n            return\n\n        # ── Pipelined path: per row-tile group H2D + decode ──\n        # Groups write disjoint staging regions at their absolute positions.\n        # Loads are issued back-to-back on load_weight_stream (no throttle);\n"}],"inter